  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Basic Sciences and Scientific Capacity Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Basic sciences form the foundation of scientific knowledge, enabling a deeper understanding of natural phenomena and driving innovation across applied fields. Through this work plan, UNESCO&#x2019;s capacity-building activities will cover a wide range of areas &#x2014; from ensuring quality science education, strengthening the research capacities of institutions, to supporting international scientific cooperation, developing scientific networks, and expanding access to scientific information and infrastructure through Open Science such as remote access to equipment. This is in addition to the preparation of Member States to adopt emerging technologies such as Quantum Sciences and Artificial Intelligence.</narrative>
  </description>
